@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 
 **Start → Save shared preset… / Load shared preset…** shares the complete gameplay setup in a versioned `.snowpreset` file: current truck/engine/winch/frame-addon/XP previews, staged edits, map-truck drafts and applied map edits, upgrade results, ownership, truck groups/tiers, region difficulty/progression, randomizer rules and workspace planning settings. Export renders drafts in an isolated workspace without applying or clearing the sender's edits. Randomization choices are stored as concrete results; loading never rerolls. The file contains Brotli-compressed copy/literal differences against preserved originals, rather than full PAKs or unchanged assets. Machine paths, installed game archives, player saves, window settings and caches are excluded.
 
-Loading checks the complete preserved initial-PAK content fingerprint and the exact original archive hash of every shared map. Use the same app build and game/original files; a matching game version alone does not prove that two modified baselines match. Select the installed map folder in Map trucks if needed. Conflicting local edits or drafts require a separate clean workspace. Load writes only a persistent staged snapshot, with before/after initial-file values visible on Start; planning settings remain unchanged until **Apply pending changes**. Editing tabs are locked while the snapshot is staged. **Discard shared preset** removes it without changing outputs. Apply verifies all baselines again, prepares every output, preserves old files/settings under `preset-history`, and rolls back completed replacements on failure. The app refreshes its planning and editor state after Apply. Pack a new initial PAK and install the separate map outputs manually.
+Loading checks the complete preserved initial-PAK content fingerprint and the exact original archive hash of every shared map. Use the same app build and game/original files; a matching game version alone does not prove that two modified baselines match. Select the installed map folder in Map trucks if needed. When local previews, pending edits, drafts, applied changes or another staged preset exist, Load warns and asks whether to replace them. No cancels loading. Yes stages the preset as a complete replacement; old pending edits are ignored while it is staged. Apply backs up and clears superseded pending stores and local outputs absent from the preset, so they cannot leak into the shared result. Discarding before Apply retains existing saved work. Original-file compatibility checks still apply. Load writes only a persistent staged snapshot, with before/after initial-file values visible on Start; planning settings remain unchanged until **Apply pending changes**. Editing tabs are locked while the snapshot is staged. **Discard shared preset** removes it without changing outputs. Apply verifies all baselines again, prepares every output, preserves old files/settings under `preset-history`, and rolls back completed replacements on failure. The app refreshes its planning and editor state after Apply. Pack a new initial PAK and install the separate map outputs manually.
 
 The same preset applied to matching originals produces the same initial and map contents. Initial PAK packing uses ordinal cache-entry ordering and fixed ZIP timestamps/attributes, so the same app build also produces byte-identical archives across workspace paths, file modification times and system cultures. For the sender to reproduce the complete exported preview, stage and apply all included previews/drafts, or load that same preset into a clean workspace. Automated checks cover cross-workspace initial/map SHA-256 equality, compact deltas, preview capture, staging/restart reads, baseline conflicts, malformed presets and rollback after a locked-file failure. Runtime behavior still requires in-game verification.
 
